    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Bright 3 bed home in a mature, convenient residential setting.\n\nA well maintained three bedroom mid terrace home extending to approx. 80 sq.m., this property offers bright, well proportioned accommodation with excellent natural light throughout.\nThe property enjoys an exceptional location within walking distance of Marshes Shopping Centre, Dundalk town centre and a full range of cafés, restaurants and retail. It offers excellent connectivity with nearby bus routes, Dundalk Train Station and quick access to the M1 for Dublin or Belfast. A choice of primary and secondary schools, leisure facilities, parks and healthcare services are all close by, making this a highly convenient and sought after setting. \n\nAn ideal choice for first time buyers or investors seeking a strong, low maintenance property.\n\nThe home includes a welcoming living room, a spacious kitchen/diner, three bedrooms and a modern bathroom. \n\nOutside, the property benefits from off street parking, a low maintenance front garden and a large enclosed rear garden, offering excellent potential for outdoor living or future landscaping.\n\nMain features:\nAlarmed\nMid Terrace property \nSecure, Low maintenance gardens\nInternet availability\nTurnkey condition\nGFCH\nuPVC double glazing throughout\nOff street parking\nEasy access to m1 motorway, bus routes and midway between Dublin and Belfast\nConvenient location with all typical amenities close by\n\nACCOMMODATION\nLaminate flooring, carpet to stairwell\n\nLiving Room\nLaminate flooring, solid fuel fire with marble and timber surround, tv point, coving, dado rail\n\nKitchen\nTiled Flooring and splashback, fitted kitchen units, electric cooker, integrated hood.\n\nBedroom 1\nlaminate flooring\n\nBedroom 2 \nLaminate flooring\n\nBedroom 3 \nLaminate flooring, built in storage\n\nMain bathroom \nTiled shower enclosure, tiled flooring, whb, toilet, electric shower\n\nConstruction\nThe property is of a typical timber frame construction with a rendered/brick finish outer leaf, uPVC double glazed windows and solid wooden front door. uPVC fascia, soffit and downpipes. Tiled pitch roof.\n\nOutside\nEntrance to the property is approached by a concrete driveway and lawned area. large enclosed rear garden.\n\n\nEssential services\nMains water\nMains sewerage\nGFCH\nOff street parking\n\nViewing\nBy appointment only\n\n\n"
      },
